ef 17592186120635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119996 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119996 #edb/ref 1045 "Further Properties of Determinants" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119996 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186120630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119996 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119996 #edb/ref 1050 660.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119996 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "5359b253-6e73-5b33-a1e8-93617de4d0e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120630 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120630 #edb/ref 1061 16227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120630 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "425217e0-d658-532e-a440-a3ddd4b953cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120630 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120631 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120631 #edb/ref 1061 16228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120631 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b7196473-0bc4-579e-90dc-f9136aa28e30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120631 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120632 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120632 #edb/ref 1061 16229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120632 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c3a5d472-bd0b-516a-aa13-594c8fc6b508" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120632 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120633 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120633 #edb/ref 1061 16230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120633 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "89f23361-1b55-5691-bba9-28621e40e324" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120633 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120634 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186120635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120634 #edb/ref 1061 16231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120634 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f7d6d5a0-3ce7-530f-a0b1-24773b682d6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120634 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186121024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120635 #edb/ref 1061 16232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120635 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eeaa9b6a-90e5-5a18-85ae-913e7cbc0f24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186120635 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186119780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121022 #edb/ref 1064 "In this topic, we will consider a few more properties of determinants. Let's start with the following important property. \n\n*The determinant of the product of two square matrices is equal to the product of the determinants.*\n\nSymbolically, if ![](images/34/34058a2a5d1de088feed7d9825ba218394c9a8bb880b046be7b47307cdd37ce1.svg) and ![](images/25/256531b7f0ddb14dd11a59a3019a3361f1607d3fe16fa6d530a461344de8f39e.svg) are both square matrices, then\n\n![](images/e5/e59b47ca5462a066093945e2698404e595a92e9e70a2b8c4f8b2f30df9c9fbf1.svg)\n\nFor instance, suppose that we want to find the determinant of the matrix ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) that is defined as follows:\n![](images/9a/9a705ea4bd482cdf83251288108b48ff5bc7354c9d51c1b710b9e734c8a32dea.svg)\n\nTo easily compute ![](images/da/dab9a65c1cba3cd9f271a1910b060e5428813107b3b54945776aab3839003d45.svg), we first compute the determinants of the two matrices and then multiply the results. Also, notice that both matrices in our product are triangular, so their determinants are given by the product of the diagonal entries:\n\n![](images/fa/fa4214541c12b0a761fd7cb17f4efc2f6b4be2c1424094483a3c2f61ab63c0a0.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121022 #edb/ref 1065 3009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121022 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5a8abcbc-c41d-5553-8b2e-daa7256d7d34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121022 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121023 #edb/ref 1064 "Another useful property of determinants is that, for any invertible matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\det(A^{-1}) = \\dfrac{1}{\\det(A)}.\n$$\n\nTo understand why the above property is true, remember that $A \\cdot A^{-1} = I$ for any invertible matrix $A.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot {A}^{-1} & =I \\\\ det(A\\cdot {A}^{-1}) & =det(I) \\\\ det(A)\\cdot det({A}^{-1}) & =1 \\\\ det({A}^{-1}) & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Important:** We can only apply the formula $\\det(A^{-1}) = \\dfrac{1}{\\det(A)}$ if $A$ is invertible, meaning that $\\det(A) \\neq 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121023 #edb/ref 1065 3010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121023 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "043b8a4a-8f67-5ae8-a7ae-bbda3fa2bdbe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121023 #edb/ref 1067 "The Determinant of an Inverse Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121024 #edb/ref 1064 "One final important property of the determinant is that it is **linear in each row and column**. For rows, for example, this means \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & det\\begin{bmatrix}⋮ & ⋮ & … & ⋮ \\\\ {◻}_{1}+{△}_{1} & {◻}_{2}+{△}_{2} & … & {◻}_{n}+{△}_{n} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & … & ⋮\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\,\\,=det\\begin{bmatrix}⋮ & ⋮ & … & ⋮ \\\\ {◻}_{1} & {◻}_{2} & … & {◻}_{n} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & … & ⋮\\end{bmatrix}+det\\begin{bmatrix}⋮ & ⋮ & … & ⋮ \\\\ {△}_{1} & {△}_{2} & … & {△}_{n} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & … & ⋮\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor instance, it's easy to check that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{-2}{\\overset{⏞}{det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}} & =det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0+3 & 4+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{4}+{{det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that this property also holds for columns:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det\\begin{bmatrix}⋯ & {◻}_{1}+{△}_{1} & ⋯ \\\\ ⋯ & {◻}_{2}+{△}_{2} & ⋯ \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ ⋯ & {◻}_{n}+{△}_{n} & ⋯\\end{bmatrix}=det\\begin{bmatrix}⋯ & {◻}_{1} & ⋯ \\\\ ⋯ & {◻}_{2} & ⋯ \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ ⋯ & {◻}_{n} & ⋯\\end{bmatrix}+det\\begin{bmatrix}⋯ & {△}_{1} & ⋯ \\\\ ⋯ & {△}_{2} & ⋯ \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ ⋯ & {△}_{n} & ⋯\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{-2}{\\overset{⏞}{det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}} & =det\\begin{bmatrix}1+0 & 2 \\\\ 0+3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={{det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{4}+{{det\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{-6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186121024 #edb/ref 1065 3011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121024 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f26cf5f4-fd6d-5502-94d6-4b34bd2568ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186121024 #edb/ref 1067 "The Linearity of the Determinant" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352065 #edb/ref 1080 "282" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352065 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352065 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "356b3816-6db1-52b5-bb62-b3c3cf31be2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352242 #edb/ref 1080 "447" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4961badc-1952-50cf-a3aa-c27c2154e001" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352358 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352358 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352358 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "59a4042a-f605-574f-a228-ff4ae6d308e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352581 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352581 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352581 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "73d447eb-1e81-51dc-b291-5725cee52d82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352586 #edb/ref 1080 "-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352586 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352586 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "74558c61-b294-5a8c-be71-44c0d3822c23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352678 #edb/ref 1080 "372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186